<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al Bu Falasah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Al Bu Falasah are a section of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-yas">Bani Yas</a> tribal confederation of the southern Gulf coast. In 1833 about 800 of them broke away from Abu Dhabi and settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubai-creek">Dubai Creek</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maktoum-bin-butti">Maktoum bin Butti</a> and Obaid bin Said, founding the Sheikhdom of Dubai. Their leading family, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-maktoum">Al Maktoum</a>, has ruled Dubai ever since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-bu-falasah.jpg" alt="Al Bu Falasah" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Dubai · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_Dubai.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
